ived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-10-09T22:51:22Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T00:39:18Z","closed_at":"2025-10-10T19:09:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproduced in v4.5.stable.official [876b29033]\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot v4.5.stable.official [876b29033] - Compatibility - Dedicated RTX 4090\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen adding a light occluder to a tileset and shining a light on it, it casts a shadow upon the tile itself. There's no way to have both a lit up tile and a shadow behind it. The two light approach doesn't work for most top-down games because the second light (that does not cast shadows) hits tiles behind corners as well.\n\n<img width=\"316\" height=\"368\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cf0ceeef-9497-4ed0-81d3-04f741a9f5d7\" />\n<img width=\"305\" height=\"365\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7c1292a8-8264-4446-ba06-bd4e0339dfe2\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a TileMapLayer\n- Add a TileSet with any tiles\n- Paint a light occluder on a tile, and place it on the map.\n- Add a PointLight2D that casts shadows\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22805924/bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"aleks-313","id":148381480,"node_id":"U_kgDOCNgfKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/148381480?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313","html_url":"https://github.com/aleks-313","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aleks-313/following{/other_user